  {
   "description": "I want to have a way to do masonry layout — with many layout possibilities — without having to use JavaScript.",
   "url": "https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/308#issuecomment-3717216253"
  },
  {
   "description": "I want a denser view of projectwallace.com's CSS analysis panels. The lengths of the panels depends on the website analyzed, so there can be big gaps if there are many prefixed selectors but none with browserhacks, for example.\n\n| before | after |\n|--------|-------|\n|    <img width=\"1171\" height=\"762\" alt=\"Project Wallace CSS analysis page. It shows 8 panels with data like tables and headings across two grid rows. Each panel has a different height. The first row has one column that is significantly shorter than the others, causing a big gap of unused space.\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5962d21c-538b-42f0-8d48-196e38afbb83\" /> |   <img width=\"1170\" height=\"762\" alt=\"Project Wallace CSS analysis page. It shows 10 panels with data like tables and headings. Each panel has a different height and all panels are packed densely together, leading to a staggered edge at the bottom of the end of the list of panels.ge\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a39978b-94ea-402b-995f-0d3b95167c62\" /> |",
   "url": "https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/308#issuecomment-4742100503"
  }
